WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.280
Two taxi firms, outside the same station.

2
00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.760
Taxi A: a fixed fee of three pounds fifty,

3
00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.210
plus one pound twenty per kilometre.

4
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:14.260
Taxi B: six pounds fixed, plus
ninety-five pence per kilometre.

5
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:18.570
Plot cost against distance:
each fare is a straight line.

6
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.740
Right now, A is cheaper.

7
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.730
But A's line is steeper.

8
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:25.210
So does B ever become the better deal?

9
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.170
And if it does, where
does the choice flip?

10
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.530
In this mission, you'll read
a line's gradient as a rate,

11
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:35.980
in pounds per kilometre, and its
y-intercept as the starting value.

12
00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:39.240
You'll write a cost as a function, C of d.

13
00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:42.070
And you'll find where
two graphs intersect.

14
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.480
Your mission: work out when
the cheaper one switches.
